Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: DispCtrl <https://github.com/HaythmKenway/DispCtrl/issues>
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: libc6 (>= 2.27), libgcc-s1 | libgcc1, libstdc++6, zlib1g, libx11-6, libxrandr2, libxi6, libxfixes3, libxcomposite1, libcairo2, libpango-1.0-0, libpangocairo-1.0-0, libfontconfig1, libice6, libsm6
Recommends: ddcutil
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/HaythmKenway/DispCtrl
Description: per-monitor brightness, dimming, night light and arrangement
 DispCtrl for Linux sets each display's brightness - external monitors over
 DDC/CI (through ddcutil) and a laptop's own panel through its backlight -
 and warms or dims any display through its gamma ramp, with a night light
 schedule kept by a small user service. A command line (dispctrl-linux) and
 a window (dispctrl-linux-gui). It also arranges the displays and adds snap
 layouts. Night light, dimming, arranging and snapping need an X11 session.
